diff --git a/CHANGELOG.rst b/CHANGELOG.rst
index 87af3c7..a75d1d3 100644
--- a/CHANGELOG.rst
+++ b/CHANGELOG.rst
@@ -7,6 +7,28 @@ Version 3.0.3 (in development)
 
 * Bump vcpkg hash for Windows wheel.
 
+* Add :func:`~cdd.polyhedron_append_halfspaces` and
+  :func:`~cdd.copy_generators_with_ids`, wrapping cddlib's new
+  ``dd_DDAppendHalfspaces`` and ``dd_CopyGeneratorsWithIds``: incrementally
+  append inequalities to an already-computed polyhedron (resuming the
+  double description method instead of recomputing from scratch), and
+  retrieve each vertex/ray together with a persistent id that survives
+  across such calls.
+
+  .. warning::
+      Requires a cddlib build that provides ``dd_DDAppendHalfspaces`` and
+      ``dd_CopyGeneratorsWithIds``. These are not yet part of any released
+      cddlib version.
+
+* Fix the Windows ``tmpfile()`` workaround (used internally for error
+  reporting and for ``str()`` on :class:`~cdd.Matrix`/:class:`~cdd.LinProg`/
+  :class:`~cdd.Polyhedron`) to also apply when compiling with MinGW, not
+  just MSVC. The workaround was previously gated on ``_MSC_VER`` alone;
+  MinGW builds fell through to plain ``tmpfile()``, which is broken on
+  Windows regardless of compiler (it tries to create the file in the root
+  of the current drive) and caused a crash the moment any of those code
+  paths ran.
+
